# Voice & Format Rules

## Resume Professional Summary
- NO first-person ("I", "I've", "I'm")
- NO contractions
- ONE paragraph, ~120 words max
- NO "Combines X with Y" or "Brings the rare combination"
- Lead with role-class noun phrase
- End with 1-2 short factual sentences

## Resume Format
- Section headers: **ALL CAPS BOLD** (not ## markdown)
- Experience: date-first in bold, then company, then location
- Education: school+location plain, bold degree
- No "References available upon request"
- No "Affiliations" → use "EXTRA-CURRICULAR"
- Current role: 5-7 bullets max
- Past roles: 4 bullets max

## Resume Bullets
- Outcomes over tech-stack detail
- Vary lead verbs (no 3 in a row same)
- Bold artifact name + metric only
- NO em dashes anywhere - use commas, hyphens, or spaced single dashes (" - ")

## Cover Letters (OPPOSITE voice from resume)
- First-person required
- Contractions required (≥1 per paragraph)
- Personal aside required (≥1 per letter)
- NO em dashes - use commas, hyphens, or spaced single dashes (" - ")
- Vary openers across letters
- Vary closers across letters
- Vary sign-offs (never default "Best regards")
- ~350-400 words

## Banned Phrases (remove on sight)
- "leveraging"
- "delve into"
- "robust"
- "comprehensive" (as praise)
- "seamless"
- "cutting-edge"
- "landscape" (unless geographic)
- "Combines X with Y"
- "Brings the rare combination"
- "I'm thrilled"
- "passionate about"

## Auditability
- Every metric must trace to PROFILE.md
- Never invent numbers
- If unsourced, stop and ask user to confirm
